<mxCell id="c676" value="External (CRM.partners, Laravel users — outside this schema)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;fontColor=#12181F;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="72" y="2075" width="700" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="c677" value="FK* = references public.users(id) or &quot;CRM&quot;.partners(id), outside this module's schema (Core-to-Core FK is allowed per CLAUDE.md §5, unlike Core-to-Vertical). Every table in this diagram also carries company_id -&gt; companies.id (§5 — intra-tenant multi-company axis, distinct from the DB-per-tenant cross-tenant boundary) but that edge is drawn only once (from accounts) for readability, not on all 49 tables. product_id/product_category_id on inv_gl_account_map and payroll_component_id on payroll_gl_account_map are deliberately soft references (plain BIGINT, no FK) into INVENTORY/PAYROLL, which are optional per-tenant modules (§3H/§3S) — these posting engines must stay inert, never fail to migrate, if one is absent. subject_type/subject_id polymorphic pointers (gl_journals, ar_invoices, ap_bills, fa_assets, inv_posting_log, payroll_posting_log) are informational only, never a real FK." style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5563;align=left;fontStyle=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="2124" width="1600" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
